# === Secrets & credentials (never commit) ===
homeassistant/secrets.yaml
**/secrets.yaml
!**/secrets.yaml.example
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!*.public.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
!*.pub

# Signal K runtime secrets / identity
**/signalk/security.json
**/signalk/applicationData/
**/signalk/serverState/
**/signalk/plugin-config-data/**/*.json.bak
**/signalk/appstore-cache/
**/signalk/plugin-config-data/kip/
# resources-provider.json (the plugin's own config) stays tracked; the
# resources/ data dir it creates alongside itself is live saved routes/
# waypoints/notes (e.g. Sisu Nav's Route -> Commit, #78) — generated
# per-server state, not source, same reasoning as kip/ above.
**/signalk/plugin-config-data/resources-provider/

# Root signalk/ is legacy/non-production (issue #4) — homeassistant/signalk/
# is the one authoritative Signal K config tree (deploy + compose mount).
# Guard against re-tracking anything there; local leftover files (node_modules,
# security.json, etc.) may still exist on disk, untracked, harmless.
/signalk/

